WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.558
Prepare five questions for the same goal you have developed through the course.

2
00:00:04.758 --> 00:00:07.982
Write the answer and a brief explanation for each.

3
00:00:08.182 --> 00:00:11.762
Define three observable criteria for the final product.

4
00:00:11.962 --> 00:00:17.117
Use QuizSplat and RubricSplat if they fit, or use the supplied worksheet.

5
00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:23.388
The goal is a coherent cycle of evidence and response, not a collection of unrelated quizzes.

6
00:00:23.588 --> 00:00:26.573
Read the two supplied sample explanations.

7
00:00:26.773 --> 00:00:31.879
Identify one strength in the weaker response and one important next action.

8
00:00:32.079 --> 00:00:35.096
Revise the answer yourself using that action.

9
00:00:35.296 --> 00:00:39.988
Check whether the revision improves the reasoning rather than only changing the wording.

10
00:00:40.188 --> 00:00:45.546
This rehearsal helps you discover whether your feedback is specific enough for a learner to use.

11
00:00:45.746 --> 00:00:48.695
Schedule a related prompt two days later.

12
00:00:48.895 --> 00:00:55.325
Change the example while retaining the thinking demand so that the learner cannot simply reproduce the original

13
00:00:55.525 --> 00:00:56.531
sentence.

14
00:00:56.731 --> 00:01:02.597
Write the result that would lead you to reteach, provide additional practice or offer an extension.

15
00:01:02.797 --> 00:01:08.595
Your deliverable is the question set, criteria, visible revision and follow-up plan.

16
00:01:08.795 --> 00:01:11.753
Use the module quiz to check your own reasoning.
